The same file has many names depending on where you stand: an absolute
path from the root of the tree, a relative path from the working
directory (\cref{sec:filesystem}).
The item shows two commands that reach the same file and asks the student
to reconcile them.
The correct answer identifies the two paths as two names for one file;
the distractors take them for different files, deny that a relative path
is legitimate, or read the absolute path as making a copy.

