Programs read text in and write text out, which is why any producer can
feed any consumer---the uniform interface (\cref{sec:composition}).
The item varies the producer while keeping the consumer invariant (a
generalisation pattern): the same [[sort]] follows two different
programs, and the student must say why that works.
The correct answer names the shared text interface; the distractors
invent special modes, conflate the two producers, or deny that the reuse
is possible.

